# Copy to .env and fill in. The Makefile loads .env, and Conductor copies
# .env* files into new workspaces. `make worktree` copies it into each task
# worktree and adds KNOWSEEK_WORKSPACE, which names that worktree's databases.
# Do not set KNOWSEEK_WORKSPACE by hand in the main checkout.

# Embedding provider. The default is ollama: real semantic search, free, local
# (`brew install ollama`, `brew services start ollama`; `make dev` and
# `make start` check it and pull the model on the first run).
# hashing is the opt-out: no semantics (matches words), needs no Ollama.
# voyage is hosted and needs VOYAGE_API_KEY.
# After a switch, run `make db-reset`. Re-ingesting does not help: ingest skips
# documents whose body is unchanged (see docs/tasks/017-re-embed-job.md).
# EMBEDDINGS_ADAPTER=ollama (default)
# EMBEDDINGS_ADAPTER=hashing

# Ollama. The model must output 1024 dimensions.
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=bge-m3
# With `docker compose --profile app up`, localhost is the container itself, so
# the app service reads APP_OLLAMA_URL instead of OLLAMA_URL. The default,
# http://host.docker.internal:11434, reaches Ollama on the host.
# APP_OLLAMA_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# Query planning (ADR 0025). passthrough, the default, searches the query as
# typed. ollama asks a small local chat model for a few focused search queries
# inside the discovery job (the original query is always searched too, and a
# failing model never fails discovery). `make dev` and `make start` pull the
# model, a download of about 1.9 GB, and load it. It uses OLLAMA_URL above.
# PLANNER_ADAPTER=passthrough (default)
# PLANNER_ADAPTER=ollama
# OLLAMA_CHAT_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b

# Voyage AI.
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=
# VOYAGE_MODEL=voyage-3.5

# SEC EDGAR: the company card ("nvda", "nvidia") reads data.sec.gov. No key, no
# account. The SEC asks automated users to say who they are (a name and a
# contact address) and blocks undeclared tools with HTTP 403 (the card is then
# stale or unavailable, and the log says so). The default below is accepted
# today; set your own if other people use your instance.
# SEC_USER_AGENT=Knowseek/0.1 (self-hosted instance)
# SEC_USER_AGENT=My Company admin@example.com

# API keys for future providers, for example:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# App container (`docker compose --profile app up --build`). See README.md.
# APP_PORT=4000                    # host port of the API, on 127.0.0.1
# APP_DB_NAME=                     # default knowseek_prod_<KNOWSEEK_WORKSPACE>
# SECRET_KEY_BASE=                 # mix phx.gen.secret; compose has an insecure local default
# PHX_HOST=localhost               # public host name, used to build URLs

# Rate limiting (ADR 0023). Behind a reverse proxy, the CIDRs whose X-Forwarded-For
# header is believed, comma-separated. Unset: the client is the socket address.
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=10.0.0.0/8
